Patch 2503: RES_SCALE=1-4 renders at that many times the guest resolution (2 = 1440p, 3 = 4K); unset or 1 = as before.

Ported from another v19 port's RES_SCALE (itself written from the v0.15 port's notes), fitted to this line: the guest
keeps its own sizes everywhere (surface clips, viewports, textures, s_d3d.width/height) and only the D3D12 resources
grow: the swap chain (bb_w/bb_h), colour targets, scene depth surfaces and the shared depth buffer. Each resource
carries its scale (sc); viewports, scissors and copy boxes are multiplied at the D3D call; WPOS is divided back in the
fragment programs through rsx_alphatest.w (= 1/scale of the bound target); a new target's guest contents are widened.
Kept at guest size: shadow maps (patch 2502 sizes them), targets under 32 px on a side (the luminance chain), and the
colour copy of a sampled depth surface (one sample per n x n block; ZCOPY_FULL=1 full size). J-Stars-specific: a new
depth-only surface is scaled unless it is a shadow map (2502's flag; one made scaled first goes back to guest size
once), because the 640x360 depth pre-pass shares its zeta with colour passes; kept at guest size it made their target
switch scale every frame (~15 renders/s). The window options stay those of patch 2500.

Tested (US disc, quick Free Battle route): RES_SCALE=2 renders at 2560x1440, intros and fight look right, Free Battle
29.54 flips/s, no scale switches (bench/feature/2026-11-09_1732-res2b; before the zeta rule 18.48,
2026-11-09_1725-res2).

